{"texts": ["Date: Oct 01,  2007 \nProposal: Regulation Z - Truth in Lending \nDocument ID: R-1286 \nDocument 1 Version: 1 \nRelease Date: 05/23/2007 \nName: Dan E Bray \nAffiliation: Standard Oil \nCategory of Commercial \nAffiliation: \nAddress: \nCity: ogden \nState: UT \nCountry: UNITED STATES \nZip: 84403 \nPostalCode: \nComments: \nIf there is any hope left in Washington, the banks will be held to the same standard as \neveryone else. They should not be permitted to be predatorial and Legally STEAL from their \nvictims/customers. I see no reason why any and every banking practice should not be in the \nopen under the light of day. I want the BANKS held responsible to the public just as other \ninstitutions are scrutenized. PLEASE MAKE THESE THIEVES AT LEAST TELL US IN \nNONE MICROSCOPIC WRITING AND/OR VERBALLY WHAT THEY ARE \nPREPARING TO DO TO US. I think that would be fair and not flat dishonest. How can a \ngovernment that regulates so much let this go unnoticed??????? You have heartings on \ngouging in the oil business, but the sector that leads in annual earnings half the time in the \nlast 15 years is left to rape it's victims continually. Please stop these predatory practices. P.S. \nAre you going to be swayed by the big money bank lobbtists that got the bankruptcy laws \nchanged in their favor. If so could you also do us, the american taxpayer(a much larger \ngroup), an equal favor and let us see what is coming at us."], "vectors": [[0.0067699747160077095, 0.04355631396174431, -0.07153035700321198, -0.04883245751261711, 0.07636650651693344, -0.03450382128357887, 0.0036179833114147186, -0.010289785452187061, -0.03642150014638901, 0.0010239207185804844, -0.049950387328863144, 0.0643812045454979, -0.013795876875519753, 0.018404627218842506, -0.04780738055706024, -0.04076835885643959, 0.010771233588457108, -0.012463697232306004, -0.08283642679452896, 0.04057629406452179, 0.08211396634578705, -0.024524008855223656, -0.02649051323533058, 0.025692196562886238,